{"jobs":[{"id":"4ef5714c-735e-4fdf-92c6-1557058737f4","title":"Project Manager, Permitting","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2024-11-19T18:02:31.242+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/4ef5714c-735e-4fdf-92c6-1557058737f4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/4ef5714c-735e-4fdf-92c6-1557058737f4/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field at minimum</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000 - $140,000 base + Equity</p>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n\n\n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field at minimum\n\n\n\nCompensation\n\n$120,000 - $140,000 base + Equity","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"514b483f-afe7-4f7d-89af-8a936aab3a8d","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"eac7bc3f-abd5-4a93-b001-259bef36d37e","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"d7b9bed7-3c24-4af5-85fd-251c1267fd54","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"7f92029e-5628-4d74-9ac5-950e84e838e4","title":"Associate Project Manager, Permitting","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-09-25T14:49:14.112+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/7f92029e-5628-4d74-9ac5-950e84e838e4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/7f92029e-5628-4d74-9ac5-950e84e838e4/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our in-house permitting team is a key function for driving fast, reliable permitting outcomes for our customers. In this role, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support our lead project managers in delivering great permitting outcomes for customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help conduct permit research with a high degree of accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in preparing permit plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with city staff on nuances and ambiguities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor permit status and ensure timely responses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide feedback to product &amp; engineering teams to help refine our software platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with permitting leadership to refine our standard operating procedures</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To be successful in this role, you are likely someone with:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years in either construction management or architecture, with a focus on project management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience applying for and obtaining construction permits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to research permit requirements with accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable interfacing city staff and navigating administrative processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communicator with a strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive problem solver</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$80,000 - $95,000 base + Equity</p>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nOur in-house permitting team is a key function for driving fast, reliable permitting outcomes for our customers. In this role, you will:\n\n - Support our lead project managers in delivering great permitting outcomes for customers\n\n - Help conduct permit research with a high degree of accuracy\n\n - Assist in preparing permit plans\n\n - Collaborate with city staff on nuances and ambiguities\n\n - Monitor permit status and ensure timely responses\n\n - Provide feedback to product & engineering teams to help refine our software platform\n\n - Work with permitting leadership to refine our standard operating procedures\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\nTo be successful in this role, you are likely someone with:\n\n - 3+ years in either construction management or architecture, with a focus on project management\n\n - Experience applying for and obtaining construction permits\n\n - Ability to research permit requirements with accuracy\n\n - Comfortable interfacing city staff and navigating administrative processes\n\n - Clear communicator with a strong attention to detail\n\n - Proactive problem solver\n\n\n\nCompensation\n\n$80,000 - $95,000 base + Equity","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$80K – $95K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$80K - $95K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"982bdb3b-319b-4f72-a8b5-216e9b61e75e","tierSummary":"$80K – $95K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1ac94857-70c6-4eba-9faf-578afd74e276","summary":"$80K – $95K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":95000},{"id":"580da6b2-48df-4683-b99e-8b86a66da2b5","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":95000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"df39cc49-bc6b-41ff-8935-cbf0ade00f64","title":"Senior/Staff Product Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-03T13:34:33.231+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"WA","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Seattle"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/df39cc49-bc6b-41ff-8935-cbf0ade00f64","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/df39cc49-bc6b-41ff-8935-cbf0ade00f64/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Pulley's first Product Manager, you’ll report directly to our CEO and partner closely with engineering and design to help shape and execute our product roadmap.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accelerate the launch of Pulley’s newest AI product offerings and operate as the main product owner between engineering, design, and the rest of the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with design and engineering to ensure alignment across product, technical requirements, and customer needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help shape how product is built at Pulley, contributing to the processes, rituals, and communication styles of a growing product team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay ahead of the curve in AI, automation, and construction tech to continuously identify areas where we can improve the permitting process.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Need to Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of shipping B2B software products end-to-end, from discovery through launch and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep customer empathy. You go talk to users before you form opinions, and you can synthesize what you learn into product decisions the team gets behind.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder instincts. You're comfortable working at granular levels of detail, making product decisions, and building. You enable the engineers and designers around you, not just direct them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity. The right solution isn't always obvious, and you're energized by that rather than unsettled by it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical fluency. You understand how software gets built, can engage meaningfully with engineers on tradeoffs, and have some familiarity with how AI/LLM products work in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">0→1 experience. You've built something from scratch and understand what it takes to go from nothing to something customers depend on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excitement to work 4x per week in our brand new, Downtown SF office!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've built or shipped an AI/LLM feature in production. You understand evals, retrieval, and what it takes to go from demo to reliable product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a regulated or operationally complex domain such as healthcare, logistics, legal, real estate, government, construction, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've shipped a product that an operations or services team actually adopted and depends on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've been a founding or early PM at a startup.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Compensation</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$180,000 - $230,000 base + Equity</p>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nAs Pulley's first Product Manager, you’ll report directly to our CEO and partner closely with engineering and design to help shape and execute our product roadmap.\n\n - Accelerate the launch of Pulley’s newest AI product offerings and operate as the main product owner between engineering, design, and the rest of the business.\n\n - Partner closely with design and engineering to ensure alignment across product, technical requirements, and customer needs.\n\n - Help shape how product is built at Pulley, contributing to the processes, rituals, and communication styles of a growing product team.\n\n - Stay ahead of the curve in AI, automation, and construction tech to continuously identify areas where we can improve the permitting process.\n\n\nNeed to Have\n\n - Proven track record of shipping B2B software products end-to-end, from discovery through launch and iteration.\n\n - Deep customer empathy. You go talk to users before you form opinions, and you can synthesize what you learn into product decisions the team gets behind.\n\n - Builder instincts. You're comfortable working at granular levels of detail, making product decisions, and building. You enable the engineers and designers around you, not just direct them.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity. The right solution isn't always obvious, and you're energized by that rather than unsettled by it.\n\n - Technical fluency. You understand how software gets built, can engage meaningfully with engineers on tradeoffs, and have some familiarity with how AI/LLM products work in production.\n\n - 0→1 experience. You've built something from scratch and understand what it takes to go from nothing to something customers depend on.\n\n - Excitement to work 4x per week in our brand new, Downtown SF office!\n\n\nNice to Have\n\n - You've built or shipped an AI/LLM feature in production. You understand evals, retrieval, and what it takes to go from demo to reliable product.\n\n - Experience in a regulated or operationally complex domain such as healthcare, logistics, legal, real estate, government, construction, or similar.\n\n - You've shipped a product that an operations or services team actually adopted and depends on.\n\n - You've been a founding or early PM at a startup.\n\n\nCompensation\n\n$180,000 - $230,000 base + Equity","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $230K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $230K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0fd3aed3-556e-4718-9091-21a5e5f74b86","tierSummary":"$180K – $230K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"101fb341-02d3-42aa-8169-363efc5cef1d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"943aafa4-eff4-42fb-b926-0bdac201d882","summary":"$180K – $230K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":230000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":230000}]}},{"id":"a2ed16fb-0532-4cc3-b13c-e3a753548820","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [Maryland]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-14T18:57:35.435+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/a2ed16fb-0532-4cc3-b13c-e3a753548820","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/a2ed16fb-0532-4cc3-b13c-e3a753548820/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>Maryland </u>to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nYou must be located in Maryland to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a0f5e311-da8f-4ab2-b4b5-e74f1638a3ea","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"97112ac3-a7f1-4d89-bd24-4d7883ad3889","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"d5dd3167-f996-4b64-9e3e-4107441fda92","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"c5e3771f-964e-4127-9bee-dee5edf57054","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [Pennsylvania]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-04T18:41:28.611+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/c5e3771f-964e-4127-9bee-dee5edf57054","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/c5e3771f-964e-4127-9bee-dee5edf57054/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>Philadelphia</u> to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nYou must be located in Philadelphia to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"7988c76d-5388-4c0b-a7d7-a103d84b0b38","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"dd518086-3c1b-4159-96cc-dd1ff2725aa7","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"2cb10e80-8306-4593-8cd8-945ef37d46c9","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"7b5ed020-ff84-4404-8357-c193bedc163f","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [New Jersey]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-14T18:57:44.286+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/7b5ed020-ff84-4404-8357-c193bedc163f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/7b5ed020-ff84-4404-8357-c193bedc163f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>New Jersey</u> to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nYou must be located in New Jersey to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2cea876a-b1d1-4cd7-a07d-125140486c1f","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"756b761c-79ed-4a35-ad5d-e0c83aab570b","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"fc17540d-88cc-4dc7-8ce1-3407bcc47e0b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"02cfa071-1153-4409-8777-f06931ee8bff","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [New York]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-14T18:57:16.555+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/02cfa071-1153-4409-8777-f06931ee8bff","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/02cfa071-1153-4409-8777-f06931ee8bff/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>New York </u> to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nYou must be located in New York  to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e98d954e-130d-40da-92e7-e1f408b706de","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"2b0889e7-67c3-419c-b565-243cfc16807c","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"35803362-7361-45c3-93f6-883626c08291","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"25c7f709-3c09-4a72-a0e4-31970e85bf11","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [California]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-24T01:45:16.596+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/25c7f709-3c09-4a72-a0e4-31970e85bf11","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/25c7f709-3c09-4a72-a0e4-31970e85bf11/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>California</u> (or the general Bay Area) to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2>Who You Are</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nYou must be located in California (or the general Bay Area) to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"34ec5f54-237d-4215-ac41-33bcd9f83eae","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"380535b2-bbef-4f7a-a4e9-5b54e569d60b","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"2145d07a-f0ce-4105-bc61-80430e2c69a1","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5987fa9e-1771-4dce-a778-df69edb8fbc8","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [Indiana]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-14T18:59:48.506+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/5987fa9e-1771-4dce-a778-df69edb8fbc8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/5987fa9e-1771-4dce-a778-df69edb8fbc8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>Indiana</u> to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nYou must be located in Indiana to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f7a1ae36-b7ec-401a-87a7-1430b61b2033","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0b33b7fc-e652-4f78-9499-c4628636bb3f","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"1fe82bd8-2dce-469f-8082-8109b6620ef8","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"3d646dca-8f17-4981-8ff2-7a8ce33d1fe6","title":"Enterprise Account Manager","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T23:55:48.579+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"NY","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/3d646dca-8f17-4981-8ff2-7a8ce33d1fe6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/3d646dca-8f17-4981-8ff2-7a8ce33d1fe6/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Pulley's second Enterprise Account Manager, you'll own a portfolio of approximately 20–40 enterprise and mid-market customers. This is a quota-carrying role responsible for driving renewals, expansion, and long-term customer success while partnering closely with our customer-facing services team to ensure customers get the most value from both our software and our permitting expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own customer relationships from onboarding through renewal.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive renewals, expansion, and long-term account growth across your portfolio.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build relationships with stakeholders at every level, from day-to-day users to executive sponsors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead executive business reviews, strategic account planning, and customer success conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with our customer-facing services team, Product, Engineering, and Sales to deliver exceptional customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring customer feedback and market insights back to the business to improve our product and customer experience.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You enjoy building long-term relationships and becoming a trusted advisor - not just another vendor.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're commercially minded and enjoy owning renewals, expansion, and long-term customer growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You thrive in ambiguous environments where priorities evolve quickly and ownership is expected.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're equally comfortable leading executive conversations and rolling up your sleeves to solve operational challenges.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You naturally collaborate across functions and bring people together to deliver exceptional customer outcomes.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Need to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3 - 5+ years of experience in Enterprise Account Management, Customer Success, or another quota-carrying commercial role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning renewals, expansion, and revenue growth within existing customer accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing complex B2B accounts with multiple stakeholders, including executive-level relationships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts and a track record of consistently achieving quota.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication, organization, and account planning skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating in a fast-moving startup environment where you're willing to do both strategic and tactical work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited to work hybrid from our New York City office.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in construction technology, property technology, or another operationally complex B2B SaaS business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering closely with customer delivery, operations, or professional services teams.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nAs Pulley's second Enterprise Account Manager, you'll own a portfolio of approximately 20–40 enterprise and mid-market customers. This is a quota-carrying role responsible for driving renewals, expansion, and long-term customer success while partnering closely with our customer-facing services team to ensure customers get the most value from both our software and our permitting expertise.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n - Own customer relationships from onboarding through renewal.\n\n - Drive renewals, expansion, and long-term account growth across your portfolio.\n\n - Build relationships with stakeholders at every level, from day-to-day users to executive sponsors.\n\n - Lead executive business reviews, strategic account planning, and customer success conversations.\n\n - Partner closely with our customer-facing services team, Product, Engineering, and Sales to deliver exceptional customer outcomes.\n\n - Bring customer feedback and market insights back to the business to improve our product and customer experience.\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You enjoy building long-term relationships and becoming a trusted advisor - not just another vendor.\n\n - You're commercially minded and enjoy owning renewals, expansion, and long-term customer growth.\n\n - You thrive in ambiguous environments where priorities evolve quickly and ownership is expected.\n\n - You're equally comfortable leading executive conversations and rolling up your sleeves to solve operational challenges.\n\n - You naturally collaborate across functions and bring people together to deliver exceptional customer outcomes.\n\n\nNEED TO HAVE\n\n - 3 - 5+ years of experience in Enterprise Account Management, Customer Success, or another quota-carrying commercial role.\n\n - Experience owning renewals, expansion, and revenue growth within existing customer accounts.\n\n - Experience managing complex B2B accounts with multiple stakeholders, including executive-level relationships.\n\n - Strong commercial instincts and a track record of consistently achieving quota.\n\n - Excellent communication, organization, and account planning skills.\n\n - Comfortable operating in a fast-moving startup environment where you're willing to do both strategic and tactical work.\n\n - Excited to work hybrid from our New York City office.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience in construction technology, property technology, or another operationally complex B2B SaaS business.\n\n - Experience partnering closely with customer delivery, operations, or professional services teams.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $180K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $180K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"396a3196-bbce-4d12-a830-93cea39cbadb","tierSummary":"OTE $120K – $180K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ff876a03-5670-47bc-982f-72404a734b5c","summary":"OTE $120K – $180K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":180000},{"id":"c53871df-c1cd-463a-9bf0-ef6b9503b746","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":180000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"37977105-82af-4cc2-a087-3c1bfa224cf0","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [Illinois]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-05T14:18:44.042+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/37977105-82af-4cc2-a087-3c1bfa224cf0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/37977105-82af-4cc2-a087-3c1bfa224cf0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>Illinois</u> to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nYou must be located in Illinois to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f8000e49-ed0d-4784-9c36-24b11865cb57","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3adc76f1-0fc9-4ed7-8c6a-a8c4b72a4602","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"5c58ce89-3f0c-4dca-9657-ef66fcff811e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5c163b8f-8946-44af-9043-e5d22f0118d8","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [Minnesota]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-19T21:07:18.091+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/5c163b8f-8946-44af-9043-e5d22f0118d8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/5c163b8f-8946-44af-9043-e5d22f0118d8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>Minnesota</u> to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nYou must be located in Minnesota to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"dcf06816-dc55-4880-beeb-56f1f444b38b","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"780aac13-7a0f-4f70-ada8-c54e44e68764","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"4c799a44-e45f-44cd-9765-eb2d0bca13bd","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"31e2cd98-89fb-4c9c-b659-dde092c2c5d8","title":"Senior/Staff Product Designer","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T13:39:02.296+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"WA","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Seattle"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/31e2cd98-89fb-4c9c-b659-dde092c2c5d8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/31e2cd98-89fb-4c9c-b659-dde092c2c5d8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in our <strong>San Francisco, CA office</strong>, reporting to our Head of Design and collaborating with our collocated <strong>design and engineering team of 15+ people</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a </strong><em><strong>product</strong></em><strong> designer</strong> who cares deeply about designing the right thing before designing the thing right</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Driven by curiosity,</strong> you find yourself obsessing over problems that \"feel weird, but I don't know why yet\"</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Craft is a core value (and one of ours)</strong> - You have an infectiously high quality bar for how the product shows up, nothing gets past your design QA, and you know how to bring others along the way</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>There is a method to your madness</strong> - you use principles and frameworks to solve problems of varying scale, knowing there's no single right approach (but there are wrong ones)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Excited about designing for work</strong> – at this point everyone uses software to do their jobs, you’re energized by making complex domains simple to work in</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You are energized by working for startups.</strong> Translation: fast paced, async collaboration via Slack, can create something from nothing, act as an owner, and hold strong opinions loosely</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and effectively communicate compelling user flows and specifications for stakeholders and engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI across the design lifecycle from desk research to high fidelity prototypes and production code</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead projects from concept to a successful launch, ensuring a high bar of execution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interface directly with customers to collect feedback on new and existing functionality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocate for the user by partnering with product and engineering on product definition and roadmap</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to and evolve the design system and product design lifecycle at Pulley</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Qualifications</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years designing software products; experience designing for enterprise or B2B products or services preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Expert with Figma designs and prototypes</em>.* Comfortable creating working prototypes with AI (must have) and collaborating with engineering to ship production code (nice to have)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Portfolio demonstrates product and visual design experience with a strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to and evangelizing a visual language for highly polished product experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successfully shipped web based products and features collaborating closely with engineering</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*<strong>We rarely use Figma at Pulley.</strong> We’re not doing this just for the sake of joining the AI bandwagon, working this way enables us to generate solutions more quickly, get clearer feedback from more detailed prototypes, and ship faster by handing off a coded solutions to engineering. AI hasn’t totally replaced our output, but a majority of the designs we deliver are not in Figma.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At the end of the day, we draw rectangles to communicate software product solutions for people to get their jobs done. You’re right for Pulley if you can draw, are curious about how we (and our customers) work, and can find creative for how we all will work in the future.</p>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nThis role is based in our San Francisco, CA office, reporting to our Head of Design and collaborating with our collocated design and engineering team of 15+ people.\n\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You're a product designer who cares deeply about designing the right thing before designing the thing right\n\n - Driven by curiosity, you find yourself obsessing over problems that \"feel weird, but I don't know why yet\"\n\n - Craft is a core value (and one of ours) - You have an infectiously high quality bar for how the product shows up, nothing gets past your design QA, and you know how to bring others along the way\n\n - There is a method to your madness - you use principles and frameworks to solve problems of varying scale, knowing there's no single right approach (but there are wrong ones)\n\n - Excited about designing for work – at this point everyone uses software to do their jobs, you’re energized by making complex domains simple to work in\n\n - You are energized by working for startups. Translation: fast paced, async collaboration via Slack, can create something from nothing, act as an owner, and hold strong opinions loosely\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and effectively communicate compelling user flows and specifications for stakeholders and engineers\n\n - Leverage AI across the design lifecycle from desk research to high fidelity prototypes and production code\n\n - Lead projects from concept to a successful launch, ensuring a high bar of execution\n\n - Interface directly with customers to collect feedback on new and existing functionality\n\n - Advocate for the user by partnering with product and engineering on product definition and roadmap\n\n - Contribute to and evolve the design system and product design lifecycle at Pulley\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 5+ years designing software products; experience designing for enterprise or B2B products or services preferred\n\n - Expert with Figma designs and prototypes.* Comfortable creating working prototypes with AI (must have) and collaborating with engineering to ship production code (nice to have)\n\n - Portfolio demonstrates product and visual design experience with a strong attention to detail\n\n - Experience contributing to and evangelizing a visual language for highly polished product experiences\n\n - Successfully shipped web based products and features collaborating closely with engineering\n   \n   \n\n*We rarely use Figma at Pulley. We’re not doing this just for the sake of joining the AI bandwagon, working this way enables us to generate solutions more quickly, get clearer feedback from more detailed prototypes, and ship faster by handing off a coded solutions to engineering. AI hasn’t totally replaced our output, but a majority of the designs we deliver are not in Figma.\n\n\n\nAt the end of the day, we draw rectangles to communicate software product solutions for people to get their jobs done. You’re right for Pulley if you can draw, are curious about how we (and our customers) work, and can find creative for how we all will work in the future.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2b01f3ca-68f3-427e-80f3-9ce7f98ed14f","tierSummary":"$180K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"49460557-e989-4f58-9e2b-496eea426fe0","summary":"$180K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"6c6f0eea-4392-4ac7-9f58-096be4edd328","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"1f994c80-131a-4f3a-af38-b7315632f924","title":"Senior Technical Recruiter","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T17:59:18.721+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"WA","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Seattle"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/1f994c80-131a-4f3a-af38-b7315632f924","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/1f994c80-131a-4f3a-af38-b7315632f924/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>🧑‍💻 </strong>The Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley is scaling fast, and we're hiring a Senior Technical Recruiter to help us hire the top talent in the market.  This isn't a high-volume, req-filling role: you'll own full-cycle technical hiring for our San Francisco office, act as a true partner to hiring managers, and help build the talent function from the ground up.  You'll set the bar for who joins Pulley, and you'll be trusted to hold that bar even under pressure to fill seats fast.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for someone who has done this before: closed engineers away from competing offers, knows the difference between a resume that reads well and a candidate who can do the work, and who isn't afraid to tell a hiring manager their process is broken.  If you take ownership of outcomes, not just activity, we want to talk to you!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>📋 Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run full-cycle on our technical roles: source, screen, and close top-tier candidates in a competitive market</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a strategic partner to hiring managers, leadership, and founders, pushing back with data and market insights when a role or process needs to change - not just executing on the tasks handed to you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and defend a rigorous, consistent bar across every stage of a pipeline so that hiring managers trust your read on a candidate as much as your own</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design an exceptional candidate experience that reflects well on Pulley, especially with fast feedback and honest communication</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring a point of view on sourcing strategy, market mapping, and competitive positioning to help us win candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our recruiting operations and infrastructure as an early hire: building process, tooling, and metrics as Pulley scales</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>👋 Who You Are</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Several years of full-cycle technical recruiting experience, ideally scaling teams at a fast-growing startup with a track record of closing competitive technical talent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in the technical landscape: you can speak credibly with engineers about their stack and their career motivations, and you know how to evaluate signal beyond a resume</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable partnering with strong-willed, high-bar hiring managers, and skilled at pushing back constructively when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized, with the ability to juggle multiple priorities without dropping details</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a builder's mindset: creative, resourceful, and biased toward action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuinely excited about Pulley's mission, and able to sell that conviction to candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eager to work on-site in downtown San Francisco 3x / week</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n🧑‍💻 THE ROLE\n\nPulley is scaling fast, and we're hiring a Senior Technical Recruiter to help us hire the top talent in the market.  This isn't a high-volume, req-filling role: you'll own full-cycle technical hiring for our San Francisco office, act as a true partner to hiring managers, and help build the talent function from the ground up.  You'll set the bar for who joins Pulley, and you'll be trusted to hold that bar even under pressure to fill seats fast.\n\nWe're looking for someone who has done this before: closed engineers away from competing offers, knows the difference between a resume that reads well and a candidate who can do the work, and who isn't afraid to tell a hiring manager their process is broken.  If you take ownership of outcomes, not just activity, we want to talk to you!\n\n \n\n\n📋 KEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Run full-cycle on our technical roles: source, screen, and close top-tier candidates in a competitive market\n\n - Act as a strategic partner to hiring managers, leadership, and founders, pushing back with data and market insights when a role or process needs to change - not just executing on the tasks handed to you\n\n - Build and defend a rigorous, consistent bar across every stage of a pipeline so that hiring managers trust your read on a candidate as much as your own\n\n - Design an exceptional candidate experience that reflects well on Pulley, especially with fast feedback and honest communication\n\n - Bring a point of view on sourcing strategy, market mapping, and competitive positioning to help us win candidates\n\n - Improve our recruiting operations and infrastructure as an early hire: building process, tooling, and metrics as Pulley scales\n\n \n\n\n👋 WHO YOU ARE\n\n - Several years of full-cycle technical recruiting experience, ideally scaling teams at a fast-growing startup with a track record of closing competitive technical talent\n\n - Fluent in the technical landscape: you can speak credibly with engineers about their stack and their career motivations, and you know how to evaluate signal beyond a resume\n\n - Comfortable partnering with strong-willed, high-bar hiring managers, and skilled at pushing back constructively when needed\n\n - Highly organized, with the ability to juggle multiple priorities without dropping details\n\n - You have a builder's mindset: creative, resourceful, and biased toward action\n\n - Genuinely excited about Pulley's mission, and able to sell that conviction to candidates\n\n - Eager to work on-site in downtown San Francisco 3x / week","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150K – $190K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150K - $190K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"2f8df203-0caf-48eb-8798-df88b3dfb499","tierSummary":"$150K – $190K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"0ec86c25-3556-4ff5-b4ec-587952497942","summary":"$150K – $190K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":190000},{"id":"9098bc03-5126-4edd-89c2-10e7f88d790e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":190000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"80238edc-61a2-4ab7-858e-e4f6a84f05e9","title":"Strategic Account Lead","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T19:03:21.551+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/80238edc-61a2-4ab7-858e-e4f6a84f05e9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/80238edc-61a2-4ab7-858e-e4f6a84f05e9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Strategic Account Lead, you'll own 1–2 of Pulley's largest enterprise accounts — you're the main point of contact for the customer and the link between what they need and what our internal teams deliver. You keep the customer confident and informed, keep our team stocked with the context it needs, and step in early when something needs attention. This role fits someone genuinely customer-obsessed: you treat the customer's goals as your own, stay a step ahead of what they'll ask for, and measure your success by theirs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is remote and designed for someone who wants to be embedded near the customer they support.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Portfolio Visibility &amp; Program Coordination:</strong> Keep a current view of your account's full project portfolio — not to manage individual projects, but to represent the program confidently, catch patterns early, and keep everyone aligned. Meet regularly with Regional Leads to check on project health, flag anything that could affect delivery, and make sure internal teams have the context they need.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer Relationship Management:</strong> Be the go-to contact for decision-makers throughout the account. Build trust through consistent, proactive communication. Lead regular check-ins and monthly account reviews, and partner with the Account Executive on QBRs and renewals. When needed, represent the customer in city and AHJ meetings alongside our Permit Ops team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Stakeholder Onboarding &amp; Program Growth:</strong> As the account grows, onboard new stakeholders on both sides — training new members of the customer's team and bringing in outside collaborators like architects and engineers of record.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Internal Resource &amp; Cross-Functional Enablement:</strong> Act as the internal voice of the customer. Turn what you're hearing from the account into clear, useful input for Regional Leads, Head of Permitting, Operations, Product, or Sales. Help unblock issues only the customer relationship can solve, and push for process improvements that make the program work better for everyone.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2>Who you are</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4–8 years of experience in project management, program management, or a related client-facing role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in construction, real estate, architecture, permitting, or a related field — enough fluency to read project status, understand permitting terminology, spot risks early, and communicate credibly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuinely customer-obsessed — you treat the customer's goals as your own, you're proactive before they have to ask, and you're energized by being the person they most trust and rely on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to go deep on a large, complex project or program — comfortable overseeing concurrent workstreams and knowing exactly when to zoom in</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communicator — you write clearly, respond quickly, and know how to translate complex updates into crisp, customer-facing language that builds confidence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building genuine relationships with stakeholders, with the presence to represent a client's interests credibly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with sharp attention to detail — you build systems to make sure things don't slip</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working cross-functionally without direct authority — you know how to align teams, route the right information to the right people, and drive outcomes through influence and collaboration</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a high-growth startup environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with project management tools (Airtable, Notion, Asana, etc.) and data dashboards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI fluency and comfort with no-code tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting large-scale commercial programs, such as national retail rollouts, big-box or large-format retail, or warehouse and distribution construction</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000 - $140,000 base + Equity</p>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs a Strategic Account Lead, you'll own 1–2 of Pulley's largest enterprise accounts — you're the main point of contact for the customer and the link between what they need and what our internal teams deliver. You keep the customer confident and informed, keep our team stocked with the context it needs, and step in early when something needs attention. This role fits someone genuinely customer-obsessed: you treat the customer's goals as your own, stay a step ahead of what they'll ask for, and measure your success by theirs.\n\nThis role is remote and designed for someone who wants to be embedded near the customer they support.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Portfolio Visibility & Program Coordination: Keep a current view of your account's full project portfolio — not to manage individual projects, but to represent the program confidently, catch patterns early, and keep everyone aligned. Meet regularly with Regional Leads to check on project health, flag anything that could affect delivery, and make sure internal teams have the context they need.\n\n - Customer Relationship Management: Be the go-to contact for decision-makers throughout the account. Build trust through consistent, proactive communication. Lead regular check-ins and monthly account reviews, and partner with the Account Executive on QBRs and renewals. When needed, represent the customer in city and AHJ meetings alongside our Permit Ops team.\n\n - Stakeholder Onboarding & Program Growth: As the account grows, onboard new stakeholders on both sides — training new members of the customer's team and bringing in outside collaborators like architects and engineers of record.\n\n - Internal Resource & Cross-Functional Enablement: Act as the internal voice of the customer. Turn what you're hearing from the account into clear, useful input for Regional Leads, Head of Permitting, Operations, Product, or Sales. Help unblock issues only the customer relationship can solve, and push for process improvements that make the program work better for everyone.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\nRequired\n\n - 4–8 years of experience in project management, program management, or a related client-facing role\n\n - Background in construction, real estate, architecture, permitting, or a related field — enough fluency to read project status, understand permitting terminology, spot risks early, and communicate credibly\n\n - Genuinely customer-obsessed — you treat the customer's goals as your own, you're proactive before they have to ask, and you're energized by being the person they most trust and rely on\n\n - Demonstrated ability to go deep on a large, complex project or program — comfortable overseeing concurrent workstreams and knowing exactly when to zoom in\n\n - Strong communicator — you write clearly, respond quickly, and know how to translate complex updates into crisp, customer-facing language that builds confidence\n\n - A track record of building genuine relationships with stakeholders, with the presence to represent a client's interests credibly\n\n - Highly organized with sharp attention to detail — you build systems to make sure things don't slip\n\n - Comfortable working cross-functionally without direct authority — you know how to align teams, route the right information to the right people, and drive outcomes through influence and collaboration\n\nNice to Have\n\n - Experience in a high-growth startup environment\n\n - Familiarity with project management tools (Airtable, Notion, Asana, etc.) and data dashboards\n\n - AI fluency and comfort with no-code tooling\n\n - Experience supporting large-scale commercial programs, such as national retail rollouts, big-box or large-format retail, or warehouse and distribution construction\n   \n   \n\nCompensation\n\n$120,000 - $140,000 base + Equity","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c93d179d-0f85-4927-9fce-2427b278aac4","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"51d34b17-13b3-4f67-9993-619ca37452f5","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"32ee3c51-475f-4461-9330-efd9b9838736","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"ae224ec4-17ac-44fa-85e0-4c568b49b27e","title":"Senior Software Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T21:38:53.906+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"WA","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Seattle"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/ae224ec4-17ac-44fa-85e0-4c568b49b27e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/ae224ec4-17ac-44fa-85e0-4c568b49b27e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will build the product that gets stuff built. You'll work closely with engineers, designers, and end-users to accelerate our product development. As a senior-level software engineer at Pulley, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own features and systems end-to-end—from talking to users and defining requirements through architecture, implementation, and iteration in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn unstructured permitting documents, city regulations, and jurisdiction workflows into fast, reliable product experiences, with AI at the core of how the product works</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build with AI agents as a daily practice—directing, reviewing, and shipping agent-driven work at high velocity while owning the quality bar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make technical and product decisions that have direct impact on our customers and their projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the bar for the engineers around you through design review, mentorship, and the standards you set in your own work</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You thrive in ambiguity—you'd rather define the right problem than execute a spec, and you're energized rather than paralyzed when the path isn't laid out</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're product-minded: you care whether the thing you built actually solved the customer's problem, and you'll talk to users to find out</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have strong opinions about quality and velocity and don't treat them as a tradeoff — you look for the tools, abstractions, and processes that buy both</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You default to ownership: when something is broken or missing, your instinct is to fix it, not to file it as someone else's problem</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Need to have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of software engineering experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of owning significant product surface end-to-end: requirements through production, including the unglamorous parts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in modern full-stack development—we use TypeScript, React, and Google Cloud; you don't need our exact stack, but you should be productive with something similar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Real experience building with AI coding agents and LLM-powered features—not just autocomplete; you've shipped work where agents did substantial implementation under your direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to architect durable systems while making pragmatic tradeoffs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in the San Francisco Bay Area and willing to work in person 4 days a week</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in construction tech, govtech, proptech, or another domain where the hard part is messy real-world documents and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing evals or otherwise making LLM-powered features reliable in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup experience at the stage where you helped build the team, not just the product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring engineers or leading technical direction across teams</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nIn this role, you will build the product that gets stuff built. You'll work closely with engineers, designers, and end-users to accelerate our product development. As a senior-level software engineer at Pulley, you will:\n\n - Own features and systems end-to-end—from talking to users and defining requirements through architecture, implementation, and iteration in production\n\n - Turn unstructured permitting documents, city regulations, and jurisdiction workflows into fast, reliable product experiences, with AI at the core of how the product works\n\n - Build with AI agents as a daily practice—directing, reviewing, and shipping agent-driven work at high velocity while owning the quality bar\n\n - Make technical and product decisions that have direct impact on our customers and their projects\n\n - Raise the bar for the engineers around you through design review, mentorship, and the standards you set in your own work\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You thrive in ambiguity—you'd rather define the right problem than execute a spec, and you're energized rather than paralyzed when the path isn't laid out\n\n - You're product-minded: you care whether the thing you built actually solved the customer's problem, and you'll talk to users to find out\n\n - You have strong opinions about quality and velocity and don't treat them as a tradeoff — you look for the tools, abstractions, and processes that buy both\n\n - You default to ownership: when something is broken or missing, your instinct is to fix it, not to file it as someone else's problem\n\n\nNEED TO HAVE\n\n - 4+ years of software engineering experience\n\n - Track record of owning significant product surface end-to-end: requirements through production, including the unglamorous parts\n\n - Fluency in modern full-stack development—we use TypeScript, React, and Google Cloud; you don't need our exact stack, but you should be productive with something similar\n\n - Real experience building with AI coding agents and LLM-powered features—not just autocomplete; you've shipped work where agents did substantial implementation under your direction\n\n - Ability to architect durable systems while making pragmatic tradeoffs\n\n - Based in the San Francisco Bay Area and willing to work in person 4 days a week\n\n\nNICE TO HAVES\n\n - Experience in construction tech, govtech, proptech, or another domain where the hard part is messy real-world documents and processes\n\n - Experience designing evals or otherwise making LLM-powered features reliable in production\n\n - Startup experience at the stage where you helped build the team, not just the product\n\n - Experience mentoring engineers or leading technical direction across teams","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $230K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $230K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"cc25fb79-7231-464b-a28d-a148aa6b0c6a","tierSummary":"Compensation $180K – $230K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e46bd87a-220b-435b-ad0c-dacb16bbb1a7","summary":"Compensation $180K – $230K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":230000},{"id":"bf2d2658-1b66-4598-9e8e-79eed17ec443","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":230000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"8be23f3a-8058-4cb6-b04b-804320c24ecd","title":"Staff Software Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T21:48:58.601+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"WA","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Seattle"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/8be23f3a-8058-4cb6-b04b-804320c24ecd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/8be23f3a-8058-4cb6-b04b-804320c24ecd/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will build the product that gets stuff built. You'll work closely with engineers, designers, and end-users to accelerate our product development. As a staff-level software engineer at Pulley, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own problem areas, not just features—define the technical direction for a domain spanning multiple product surfaces, and carry it from ambiguity through architecture to shipped, iterated-on product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn unstructured permitting documents, city regulations, and jurisdiction workflows into fast, reliable product experiences, with AI at the core of how the product works</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build with AI agents as a daily practice—directing, reviewing, and shipping agent-driven work at high velocity while owning the quality bar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make the technical bets that determine what Pulley can build next year, not just this quarter—and own the consequences of those bets in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Multiply the engineers around you: set technical direction others build within, mentor senior engineers toward larger scope, and make the whole team faster through the systems, standards, and abstractions you create</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You thrive in ambiguity—you'd rather define the right problem than execute a spec, and you're energized rather than paralyzed when the path isn't laid out</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're product-minded: you care whether the thing you built actually solved the customer's problem, and you'll talk to users to find out</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have strong opinions about quality and velocity and don't treat them as a tradeoff — you look for the tools, abstractions, and processes that buy both</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You default to ownership at organizational scale: when something is broken or missing—a system, a process, a gap between teams—your instinct is to fix it, and you don't need permission or a mandate to start</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Need to have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of software engineering experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of owning a significant technical domain end-to-end: from \"this is somebody's problem\" through architecture, delivery, and production ownership, including the unglamorous parts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in modern full-stack development—we use TypeScript, React, and Google Cloud; you don't need our exact stack, but you should be productive with something similar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Real experience building with AI coding agents and LLM-powered features—not just autocomplete; you've shipped work where agents did substantial implementation under your direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to architect durable systems while making pragmatic tradeoffs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience mentoring engineers or setting technical direction that other engineers built within</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in the San Francisco Bay Area and willing to work in person 4 days a week</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in construction tech, govtech, proptech, or another domain where the hard part is messy real-world documents and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing evals or otherwise making LLM-powered features reliable in production</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience as the most senior engineer in a domain—being the person others escalated to when nobody knew the answer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup experience at the stage where you helped build the team, not just the product</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nIn this role, you will build the product that gets stuff built. You'll work closely with engineers, designers, and end-users to accelerate our product development. As a staff-level software engineer at Pulley, you will:\n\n - Own problem areas, not just features—define the technical direction for a domain spanning multiple product surfaces, and carry it from ambiguity through architecture to shipped, iterated-on product\n\n - Turn unstructured permitting documents, city regulations, and jurisdiction workflows into fast, reliable product experiences, with AI at the core of how the product works\n\n - Build with AI agents as a daily practice—directing, reviewing, and shipping agent-driven work at high velocity while owning the quality bar\n\n - Make the technical bets that determine what Pulley can build next year, not just this quarter—and own the consequences of those bets in production\n\n - Multiply the engineers around you: set technical direction others build within, mentor senior engineers toward larger scope, and make the whole team faster through the systems, standards, and abstractions you create\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You thrive in ambiguity—you'd rather define the right problem than execute a spec, and you're energized rather than paralyzed when the path isn't laid out\n\n - You're product-minded: you care whether the thing you built actually solved the customer's problem, and you'll talk to users to find out\n\n - You have strong opinions about quality and velocity and don't treat them as a tradeoff — you look for the tools, abstractions, and processes that buy both\n\n - You default to ownership at organizational scale: when something is broken or missing—a system, a process, a gap between teams—your instinct is to fix it, and you don't need permission or a mandate to start\n\n\nNEED TO HAVE\n\n - 8+ years of software engineering experience\n\n - Track record of owning a significant technical domain end-to-end: from \"this is somebody's problem\" through architecture, delivery, and production ownership, including the unglamorous parts\n\n - Fluency in modern full-stack development—we use TypeScript, React, and Google Cloud; you don't need our exact stack, but you should be productive with something similar\n\n - Real experience building with AI coding agents and LLM-powered features—not just autocomplete; you've shipped work where agents did substantial implementation under your direction\n\n - Ability to architect durable systems while making pragmatic tradeoffs\n\n - Experience mentoring engineers or setting technical direction that other engineers built within\n\n - Based in the San Francisco Bay Area and willing to work in person 4 days a week\n\n\nNICE TO HAVES\n\n - Experience in construction tech, govtech, proptech, or another domain where the hard part is messy real-world documents and processes\n\n - Experience designing evals or otherwise making LLM-powered features reliable in production\n\n - Experience as the most senior engineer in a domain—being the person others escalated to when nobody knew the answer\n\n - Startup experience at the stage where you helped build the team, not just the product","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $280K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $280K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"d3cf465e-aada-4ec8-a2fc-673d64598be8","tierSummary":"$220K – $280K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7686584f-f2da-4a4a-be7a-0644b56c87e0","summary":"$220K – $280K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":280000},{"id":"071b2a8b-a530-49b9-bcde-2ca2357c0a76","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":280000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"194391b6-67d3-4624-9cc6-38f4bff16009","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [Arkansas]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T16:58:15.195+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/194391b6-67d3-4624-9cc6-38f4bff16009","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/194391b6-67d3-4624-9cc6-38f4bff16009/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in <u>Arkansas</u> to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nYou must be located in Arkansas to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n   \n\nWho You Are\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"4188c396-0fa3-4f8f-a2b2-9541a27f3f96","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"9ec8b486-5ff7-42fb-ac2f-4101ffec7032","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"daacf9b3-2535-4ed9-ad12-82800f13b4c2","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"a74f5ae7-d489-4a46-937b-399ad584177f","title":"Sales Development Representative","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-05T16:40:43.925+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"NY","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/a74f5ae7-d489-4a46-937b-399ad584177f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/a74f5ae7-d489-4a46-937b-399ad584177f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><h2> The Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an SDR at Pulley, you’ll be on the front lines of our go-to-market efforts, engaging prospective customers and generating new sales opportunities. You’ll learn from experienced SDRs and Account Executives, while also gaining direct exposure to the founders and the permitting challenges we’re solving. It’s a great opportunity to build sales skills, deepen your industry knowledge, and be part of the growth of our sales organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help construction teams break ground faster</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and identify potential customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build our sales pipeline through outbound emails and cold calls to developers, owners, architects, and general contractors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop critical sales skills including meeting preparation, follow-up, and closing techniques</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent our company at industry events to develop connections in new and existing markets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to defining and refining our sales best practices</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Who You Are</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring intelligence, curiosity, and drive to succeed in an early stage tech startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relish working towards goals and quotas</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable making cold calls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quickly learn new technologies and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute prospecting plans for market development with the help of the revenue team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited to work from our NYC office</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\n THE ROLE\n\nAs an SDR at Pulley, you’ll be on the front lines of our go-to-market efforts, engaging prospective customers and generating new sales opportunities. You’ll learn from experienced SDRs and Account Executives, while also gaining direct exposure to the founders and the permitting challenges we’re solving. It’s a great opportunity to build sales skills, deepen your industry knowledge, and be part of the growth of our sales organization.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Help construction teams break ground faster\n\n - Research and identify potential customers\n\n - Build our sales pipeline through outbound emails and cold calls to developers, owners, architects, and general contractors\n\n - Develop critical sales skills including meeting preparation, follow-up, and closing techniques\n\n - Represent our company at industry events to develop connections in new and existing markets\n\n - Contribute to defining and refining our sales best practices\n\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - Bring intelligence, curiosity, and drive to succeed in an early stage tech startup\n\n - Relish working towards goals and quotas\n\n - Comfortable making cold calls\n\n - Quickly learn new technologies and processes\n\n - Develop and execute prospecting plans for market development with the help of the revenue team\n\n - Excited to work from our NYC office","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$70K – $90K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$70K - $90K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1ce56cd8-ed38-4776-a9fd-92be4bcf3e97","tierSummary":"On Target Earnings $70K – $90K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"8aec46da-abf1-473a-919a-51f7d1b80cfe","summary":"On Target Earnings $70K – $90K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":70000,"maxValue":90000},{"id":"7d8c9042-a670-4294-8240-be8144dd3dab","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":70000,"maxValue":90000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"717df72e-e10b-4f6b-bfbe-bb85cf057f99","title":"Head of Legal","department":"Business Operations","team":"Business Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T20:53:05.301+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"NY","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/717df72e-e10b-4f6b-bfbe-bb85cf057f99","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/717df72e-e10b-4f6b-bfbe-bb85cf057f99/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Pulley's first Head of Legal, you'll build and own our commercial legal function, taking on the legal and contract work our team has been absorbing as we've grown, and putting real infrastructure behind it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the legal processes, templates, and playbooks Pulley needs as it scales; much of this doesn't exist yet, so you'll be creating it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise leadership on corporate legal matters and flag risk before it becomes a problem.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with co-founders and cross functional leaders to help shape new products and service lines, weighing in early on legal and strategic considerations as we expand into new markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage relationships with outside counsel for specialized needs outside your core focus (e.g., litigation, M&amp;A, IP).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a trusted legal partner to teams across the company, translating legal complexity into clear, actionable guidance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end drafting, review, and negotiation of customer, vendor, and partner contracts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Sales and Revenue teams to structure deals and unblock negotiations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're commercially minded: you see your role as helping the business move faster, not just minimizing risk.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're comfortable being the first legal hire and building a function from scratch, without a playbook handed to you.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You default to pragmatic, business-friendly solutions over rigid process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You communicate clearly with non-lawyers and build trust quickly across functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're energized by high ownership and ambiguity in a fast-moving startup environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Need to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–9 years of experience in corporate/commercial legal work, ideally with a mixture of experience at a top startup-focused law firm with experience working in-house.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in general corporate law, tech transactions, and commercial contracts, ideally supporting emerging companies, venture-backed startups, or growth-stage companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong track record in commercial contracting: drafting and negotiating customer, vendor, and partner agreements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">J.D. from an accredited law school and active bar admission.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent judgment on when to solve something yourself versus loop in outside counsel.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating as a generalist, not a narrow specialist.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior in-house experience at a startup or growth-stage technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting corporate governance or financing-related work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to the construction, real estate, or proptech industries.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nAs Pulley's first Head of Legal, you'll build and own our commercial legal function, taking on the legal and contract work our team has been absorbing as we've grown, and putting real infrastructure behind it.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n - Build the legal processes, templates, and playbooks Pulley needs as it scales; much of this doesn't exist yet, so you'll be creating it.\n\n - Advise leadership on corporate legal matters and flag risk before it becomes a problem.\n\n - Partner closely with co-founders and cross functional leaders to help shape new products and service lines, weighing in early on legal and strategic considerations as we expand into new markets.\n\n - Manage relationships with outside counsel for specialized needs outside your core focus (e.g., litigation, M&A, IP).\n\n - Act as a trusted legal partner to teams across the company, translating legal complexity into clear, actionable guidance.\n\n - Own end-to-end drafting, review, and negotiation of customer, vendor, and partner contracts.\n\n - Partner closely with Sales and Revenue teams to structure deals and unblock negotiations.\n\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You're commercially minded: you see your role as helping the business move faster, not just minimizing risk.\n\n - You're comfortable being the first legal hire and building a function from scratch, without a playbook handed to you.\n\n - You default to pragmatic, business-friendly solutions over rigid process.\n\n - You communicate clearly with non-lawyers and build trust quickly across functions.\n\n - You're energized by high ownership and ambiguity in a fast-moving startup environment.\n\n\n\n\nNEED TO HAVE\n\n - 6–9 years of experience in corporate/commercial legal work, ideally with a mixture of experience at a top startup-focused law firm with experience working in-house.\n\n - Background in general corporate law, tech transactions, and commercial contracts, ideally supporting emerging companies, venture-backed startups, or growth-stage companies.\n\n - Strong track record in commercial contracting: drafting and negotiating customer, vendor, and partner agreements.\n\n - J.D. from an accredited law school and active bar admission.\n\n - Excellent judgment on when to solve something yourself versus loop in outside counsel.\n\n - Comfort operating as a generalist, not a narrow specialist.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Prior in-house experience at a startup or growth-stage technology company.\n\n - Experience supporting corporate governance or financing-related work.\n\n - Exposure to the construction, real estate, or proptech industries.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$220K – $300K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$220K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"fb3690b4-f9a8-438f-9c4c-ffd399a70cc7","tierSummary":"$220K – $300K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c1d69849-e39b-4d52-9331-e0f8772644d6","summary":"$220K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"b3605763-e6fc-436b-b0f3-8d0d58530276","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":220000,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"d63dc75b-f134-4a98-9b54-4f74ff8b6d7b","title":"Enterprise Account Executive","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-05T19:37:31.860+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"NY","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/d63dc75b-f134-4a98-9b54-4f74ff8b6d7b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/d63dc75b-f134-4a98-9b54-4f74ff8b6d7b/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role you will</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the Full Sales Cycle: </strong>Take qualified opportunities from SDRs and your own outreach and lead them through discovery, solutioning, negotiation, and close with a focus on delivering value at every stage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive New Business and Expand Existing Accounts:</strong> Convert qualified leads into customers, then grow those accounts by identifying upsell opportunities, new use cases, and wider adoption.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Execute Strategic Outreach: </strong>Collaborate with SDRs on targeted outreach strategies, account prioritization, and follow-up to ensure a steady flow of high-quality pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communicate Value to Senior Stakeholders: </strong>Deliver clear, tailored pitches decision-makers, aligning product capabilities with business needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Cross-Functionally: </strong>Partner with permitting, marketing and product teams to shape demos, proposals, and customer experiences that drive results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Continuously Improve: </strong>Share insights from the field to help refine messaging, evolve the product, and strengthen sales processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hit Your Number: </strong>Consistently meet or exceed your revenue targets while maintaining strong forecast accuracy and a focus on long-term customer success.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Need to have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistent top performer in previous organizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of AE Experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with <em>some</em> sales methodology (MEDDPICC, BANT, Sandler, etc)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team player mentality, adept at working cross-functionally and within sales org</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear-eyed regarding the hustle, attitude, intellectual curiosity and flexibility needed to thrive in an early stage environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Great communicator with exceptional writing, presentation, and interpersonal skills, paired with strong organization and time management to effectively manage priorities and build trust across stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hybrid schedule - In office Monday and Wednesday in FiDi.</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to haves</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Has worked into construction or construction-adjacent industry</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Early stage startup experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eager to work hybrid in Manhattan</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nIn this role you will\n\n - Own the Full Sales Cycle: Take qualified opportunities from SDRs and your own outreach and lead them through discovery, solutioning, negotiation, and close with a focus on delivering value at every stage.\n\n - Drive New Business and Expand Existing Accounts: Convert qualified leads into customers, then grow those accounts by identifying upsell opportunities, new use cases, and wider adoption.\n\n - Execute Strategic Outreach: Collaborate with SDRs on targeted outreach strategies, account prioritization, and follow-up to ensure a steady flow of high-quality pipeline.\n\n - Communicate Value to Senior Stakeholders: Deliver clear, tailored pitches decision-makers, aligning product capabilities with business needs.\n\n - Collaborate Cross-Functionally: Partner with permitting, marketing and product teams to shape demos, proposals, and customer experiences that drive results.\n\n - Continuously Improve: Share insights from the field to help refine messaging, evolve the product, and strengthen sales processes.\n\n - Hit Your Number: Consistently meet or exceed your revenue targets while maintaining strong forecast accuracy and a focus on long-term customer success.\n\n\n\nNeed to have\n\n - Consistent top performer in previous organizations\n\n - 4+ years of AE Experience\n\n - Experience with some sales methodology (MEDDPICC, BANT, Sandler, etc)\n\n - Team player mentality, adept at working cross-functionally and within sales org\n\n - Clear-eyed regarding the hustle, attitude, intellectual curiosity and flexibility needed to thrive in an early stage environment\n\n - Great communicator with exceptional writing, presentation, and interpersonal skills, paired with strong organization and time management to effectively manage priorities and build trust across stakeholders.\n\n - Hybrid schedule - In office Monday and Wednesday in FiDi.\n\n\n\nNice to haves\n\n - Has worked into construction or construction-adjacent industry\n\n - Early stage startup experience\n\n - Eager to work hybrid in Manhattan","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $300K • Offers Equity • OTE","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3f77c819-be10-4dc4-b91e-8ffbabddd05a","tierSummary":"OTE $200K – $300K • Offers Equity • OTE","title":null,"additionalInformation":"OTE","components":[{"id":"b76ff1da-f643-4ee5-a1ba-1e108cb0a1be","summary":"OTE $200K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"850e2151-2044-4165-941c-74d6de75c44d","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"dc633912-e23d-4d7c-b3bb-3d13a5dc7d98","title":"Head of Business Development and Partnerships","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T22:18:53.770+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"NY","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/dc633912-e23d-4d7c-b3bb-3d13a5dc7d98","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/dc633912-e23d-4d7c-b3bb-3d13a5dc7d98/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Pulley's Head of Business Development and Partnerships, you'll build and own our channel partner program from the ground up, finding, recruiting, and enabling partners who bring business to Pulley across architecture, luxury retail, data centers, and other commercial verticals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work alongside Founders and Marketing team to exhibit Pulley’s Brand in highest visibility channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and recruit channel partners who can bring Pulley new business, working across industries and geographies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Close and onboard new partners, then enable them with the tools, positioning, and support they need to represent Pulley well.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hand off partner-sourced opportunities to our Sales team and work closely with Marketing to convert partnerships into real pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and grow long-term partner relationships, acting as their primary point of contact at Pulley.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the playbook for partner sourcing, enablement, and management as you go; there isn't one yet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring market feedback from partners back into the business to sharpen our positioning and go-to-market strategy.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're an entrepreneurial builder who thrives creating a program from scratch, not maintaining an existing one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a nose for finding the right nodes of influence and turning relationships into revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're comfortable with ambiguity and figure things out without a playbook.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can evangelize Pulley's value — you're a strong communicator who speaks the customer's language.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You collaborate naturally across Sales and Marketing to convert relationships into pipeline.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Need to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in business development, channel partnerships, or strategic alliances within a B2B, real estate, or construction-adjacent industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background at a firm like CBRE (Global Workplace Solutions, Project Management) or JLL (Portfolio, Project Delivery Services), or similar — selling technology or services through corporate real estate accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building a partner or channel program from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Director-level experience, comfortable with a comp structure balancing base and variable compensation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent relationship-building, negotiation, and cross-functional collaboration skills.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience selling into architecture, luxury retail, or data center verticals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Existing network within CBRE, JLL, or similar global real estate services firms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering closely with marketing to generate co-branded content and pipeline.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nAs Pulley's Head of Business Development and Partnerships, you'll build and own our channel partner program from the ground up, finding, recruiting, and enabling partners who bring business to Pulley across architecture, luxury retail, data centers, and other commercial verticals.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n - Work alongside Founders and Marketing team to exhibit Pulley’s Brand in highest visibility channels\n\n - Identify and recruit channel partners who can bring Pulley new business, working across industries and geographies.\n\n - Close and onboard new partners, then enable them with the tools, positioning, and support they need to represent Pulley well.\n\n - Hand off partner-sourced opportunities to our Sales team and work closely with Marketing to convert partnerships into real pipeline.\n\n - Own and grow long-term partner relationships, acting as their primary point of contact at Pulley.\n\n - Build the playbook for partner sourcing, enablement, and management as you go; there isn't one yet.\n\n - Bring market feedback from partners back into the business to sharpen our positioning and go-to-market strategy.\n\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You're an entrepreneurial builder who thrives creating a program from scratch, not maintaining an existing one.\n\n - You have a nose for finding the right nodes of influence and turning relationships into revenue.\n\n - You're comfortable with ambiguity and figure things out without a playbook.\n\n - You can evangelize Pulley's value — you're a strong communicator who speaks the customer's language.\n\n - You collaborate naturally across Sales and Marketing to convert relationships into pipeline.\n\n\n\n\nNEED TO HAVE\n\n - Experience in business development, channel partnerships, or strategic alliances within a B2B, real estate, or construction-adjacent industry.\n\n - Background at a firm like CBRE (Global Workplace Solutions, Project Management) or JLL (Portfolio, Project Delivery Services), or similar — selling technology or services through corporate real estate accounts.\n\n - A track record of building a partner or channel program from the ground up.\n\n - Director-level experience, comfortable with a comp structure balancing base and variable compensation.\n\n - Excellent relationship-building, negotiation, and cross-functional collaboration skills.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience selling into architecture, luxury retail, or data center verticals.\n\n - Existing network within CBRE, JLL, or similar global real estate services firms.\n\n - Experience partnering closely with marketing to generate co-branded content and pipeline.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $300K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $300K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"43cb7df9-d4cf-46fe-97df-e709986e4b30","tierSummary":"OTE: $200K – $300K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"831f37b5-9b7e-4136-8bee-bed3d204a663","summary":"OTE: $200K – $300K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":300000},{"id":"f5049665-0e6f-4717-badb-8a40b5e1575b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":300000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"6f6ed2f7-998c-4966-959b-1eff94a56c69","title":"Project Manager, Permitting [San Francisco]","department":"Permit Operations","team":"Permit Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T16:11:49.096+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"WA","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Seattle"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/6f6ed2f7-998c-4966-959b-1eff94a56c69","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/withpulley/6f6ed2f7-998c-4966-959b-1eff94a56c69/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Pulley</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.<br /><br /></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>You must be located in the Bay Area to be considered for this role.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Permitting Expertise:</strong> Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advise Clients:</strong> Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate with Municipalities:</strong> Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage Projects:</strong> Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate Across Teams:</strong> Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h2>Who You Are</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Professional Experience</strong>: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge</strong>: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interpersonal Skills</strong>: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency</strong>: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Pulley\n\nPulley helps the country’s top architects, builders, and retailers speed up every project in their portfolio. With AI-powered permitting intelligence and expert guidance, we eliminate costly delays and bring predictability across the full lifecycle of commercial projects. \n\nToday, permitting is the slowest, most uncertain part of building, spread across 19,000+ jurisdictions with different rules, timelines, and surprises. Pulley gives project teams the clarity and predictability they need to move from planning to opening without delays.\n\nWe support rollout programs for brands like J.Crew, Solidcore, and Hibbett Sports, as well as major data center buildouts, EV charging networks, and other commercial projects. Our platform dramatically reduces approval timelines, improves forecasting accuracy, and removes thousands of hours of manual work from design and construction teams.\n\nFounded in 2021, Pulley combines deep permitting expertise with purpose-built AI from people who have created products used by millions. We’re backed by CRV, Susa Ventures, Fifth Wall, and leaders from Plaid, Segment, ServiceTitan, and Procore.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nYou must be located in the Bay Area to be considered for this role.\n\nProject Managers are essential to success. As a Project Manager, you are the key link between clients and the intricate permitting landscape. Your work ensures that projects progress smoothly, overcoming regulatory hurdles, and collaborating with municipal officials to speed up approvals. Your expertise and proactive problem-solving directly impact project timelines, making you a critical part of our mission to transform construction.\n\nIn this role, you’ll play a pivotal part in shaping our permitting operations and work closely with leadership, product, and engineering teams to ensure continuous improvement in how we deliver results. Your contributions will help refine best practices and workflows, pushing the industry forward and enabling our clients to build faster and more effectively.\n\n \n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Permitting Expertise: Gain a deep understanding of local permitting rules across various markets, focusing on streamlining complex processes.\n\n - Advise Clients: Act as a trusted advisor, guiding clients through intricate approval processes to achieve fast and efficient outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Municipalities: Build and maintain strong relationships with municipal staff, working together to accelerate approval times.\n\n - Manage Projects: Oversee multiple permitting projects simultaneously, ensuring that each hits key milestones and moves swiftly to completion while anticipating and resolving potential permitting roadblocks, ensuring projects stay on track.\n\n - Collaborate Across Teams: Work with internal teams from product, engineering, and leadership to continuously improve Pulley’s platform and enhance the client experience.\n   \n    \n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - Professional Experience: 6+ years in architecture, construction, or permitting, with demonstrated involvement in various permitting processes.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong familiarity with local building codes, zoning regulations, and permitting processes.\n\n - Interpersonal Skills: Excellent communication abilities and talent for building strong relationships with clients and municipal officials.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Skilled in using relevant software tools and adaptable in learning new systems that enhance operational efficiency.\n\n - Bachelor's Degree in Architecture or closely related field","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"34ec5f54-237d-4215-ac41-33bcd9f83eae","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"380535b2-bbef-4f7a-a4e9-5b54e569d60b","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"2145d07a-f0ce-4105-bc61-80430e2c69a1","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}